course: dictionary
lesson: 6443
title: Name: one word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Name» can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, it is the word we call a person, pet, place or thing: «LEGO is a Danish company, and its name comes from the Danish "leg godt".» Here, name is the word the company is called.
explain: As a verb, to name something means to give it a name, or to say what it is. «Name three colours» asks you to say what three colours are, not to give them names. Look at the words around it to see which job it is doing.
explain: Sometimes name means what people think of you, as in «a good name». Ask yourself: is this a thing, or an action? The context will tell you which meaning fits.
fact: A name is the word we call a person, pet, place or thing.
fact: «Named after» means it has the name of someone or something else, as in «Pentecostal churches are named after Pentecost».
fact: «The same piece has three names: a meteoroid in space, a meteor while it glows in the air, and a meteorite if it lands on the ground.» The name changes depending on where the piece is.
fact: «Call someone names» means to be rude to them. «First name» is the name given to you, and «last name» is your family name.
fact: The word name can be a noun or a verb, so check the words around it to see which one it is.
exercise: «LEGO is a Danish company, and its name comes from the Danish "leg godt".» In this sentence, what is name? | To give the company a name | A good name | *The word we call the company | To say what the company is
exercise: «Name three colours.» What does name mean here? | *To say what three colours are | To paint three colours | A colour called a name | To give a new name to a colour
exercise: «She has a good name at school.» What does name mean here? | A word we call a person | *What people think of her | To give a name to the school | A school bell
test: «Pentecostal churches are named after Pentecost.» What does named after mean? | To be forgotten by everyone | To be rude to someone | To say what something is | *Given the name of someone or something else
test: What kind of word is name in «Name the shape»? | *Verb | Adverb | Noun | Adjective
exam: «The same piece has three names: a meteoroid, a meteor and a meteorite.» Why does it have three names? | It was named three times by three different people | *Its name changes depending on where it is | It is really three different pieces | All three names mean the same thing, so it is a mistake
